===Etymology 2===
Back-formation from {{m|en|cockroach}}, as if it were a compound
Marijuana-related meanings by similarity of appearance of the butt, attested since the 1930s.

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|cockroach}}{{lb|en|US}} A [[cockroach]].
# {{lb|en|US|slang|smoking}} The [[butt]] of a marijuana [[cigarette]].
# {{lb|en|US|slang|smoking}} An entire [[marijuana]] [[cigarette]], [[blunt]], or [[joint]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1957|author=Alfred Maund|title=The Big Boxcar|location=Urbana|publisher=University of Illinois Press|isbn=0252067541|page=106|passage=In his half hour of free time between brooms it was Willie's custom to smoke his lunch in an alleyway. He'd take just half a '''roach''', only enough to make him feel a new day was starting, no more no less.}}
# {{lb|en|UK|slang|smoking}} The [[filter]] of a rolled [[cigarette]] or [[joint]], made from card or paper.
#* {{RQ:Smith White Teeth|year=2001|page=292|passage=Last toke is the yellowing fabric of the '''roach''', containing the stuff that is less than tobacco.}}

